{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790323743,"nonce":"VRVsYtA70k6eDtM2BhGbJK0L8dM=","title":"Tiered: HIR pipeline repeats outside the first optimisation of a function or region","message":"The user's rule: a function's (or region's) HIR is optimised once and every later tier, LLVM included, compiles that optimised HIR. LLVMJitBackend::compile_function itself runs no HIR pass, but three paths that feed LLVM repeat the pipeline, and two send it HIR other than the stored optimised body.\n\n1. A region outlined from a library (snapshot-finished) function is cut from HIR already through the pipeline; optimize_extra runs the whole run_interp_safe_opts_cached over it again and promote_outlined_region sends the result to LLVM. Runtime logs: zb_list_sort_ptr$resume1 took 44 pass invocations and 3.8 ms in pyflate; zb_list_repeat_i64 and zb_list_from_wide_u8 the same in raytrace.\n2. optimize_body races: the optimized_bodies check comes before the scratch lock and the scratch guard drops before or_insert, so a second caller (the call-count broker or the interpreter's lazy getter, neither serialised by first_compiles) resets `optimized` on the scratch's already optimised copy and runs the whole pipeline again. The finished-function branch runs boxes/licm/cse unlocked, so twice too.\n3. The same loop of a program function could be outlined, and its region optimised, once per request rather than once per (bead, body tag, loop ordinal).\n4. Wrong source, not a rerun: optimize_function and record_call read entry.body(), the lowered module body of a lazy function; closure promotion (ZYNTAX_LLVM_CLOSURE_PROMOTION=1 / ZYNTAX_LLVM_MCJIT=0) takes callees lowered from module_context.\n5. reload_module never touched optimized_bodies; the interpreter's getter and optimize_body read it before any swapped body, so a reloaded lazy function could still hand out its pre-reload optimised body.\n\nCost measured by the investigation: 0 to 43 ms per run, 1 to 5% of request-to-install time.\n\nFix: optimized_bodies becomes one OnceLock cell per lazy function, filled by the first caller under the scratch lock (finishing step included); every compile path reads tier_body (swapped, else cell, else module). A region cut from optimised HIR takes the finishing step plus cfg_simplify and phi_prune, never the pipeline; a region cut from a lowered body keeps its single run, claimed once per (bead, tag, ordinal). ZyntaxFunctionDef carries the Arc so LLVM compiles the body it is handed. Reload swaps in filled cells and rollback restores them. Tests: crates/compiler/tests/optimized_once.rs and optimized_once_race.rs (opt_audit counters).","files":null}]}